From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:07:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] operations: borrow var-scoped declarations instead of cloning
 them

VarScopedDeclarations handed back owned copies of every top-level
function declaration, body and all, and both the scope analyzer and the
bytecompiler then cloned them again into functionsToInitialize. For a
bundle that is one or two full copies of its syntax tree held alongside
the original while compiling: a third of react-dom's compile peak. The
callers only ever read them, so return references into the tree.
---
